   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1. The Cabinet endorsed and submitted to parliament in June 2024 the Water Resources Bill to promote integrated water resource management at the river basin level, preserve surface and ground water resources, control water pollution, and foster sustainable use of water and water related materials.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.2. (i) The Cabinet approved River and Water Related Disaster Management National Policy in December 2023 to promote integrated water resource management including multipurpose projects in river basins, and to enhance disaster preparedness by facilitating the adoption of remote sensing system, geographical information system, open-source technology, and forecast based financing; and (ii) NDRRMA approved construction design standards, including financial incentives for its adoption, to promote the use of indigenous construction materials for recovery and reconstruction.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.3. (i) The Cabinet approved the Wildlife-friendly Infrastructure Development Directives in April 2022 to enhance balance between conservation needs and infrastructure development; and (ii) transport sector started piloting the directives in May 2023.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.4. (i) MOEWRI approved Renewable Energy Subsidy Operational Procedures effective December 2022 to promote energy security through the adoption of small and micro hydropower, biogas, biomass, solar, and wind; and (ii) the Cabinet endorsed and submitted in June 2024 to the parliament a REEE bill to strengthen the mandate of AEPC to promote renewable energy and enhance energy efficiency.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.5. The Parliament approved Finance Act 2024, which imposed green tax on imported petroleum products and coal effective July 2024 in line with its NDC commitments to reduce carbon emissions and promote low carbon transition.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.6. The Cabinet approved Green Hydrogen Policy 2024 on 18 January 2024 to promote hydrogen energy as a clean and alternative energy source to petroleum fuel and natural gas.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">14 Nov 2024 | News Release: https://www.adb.org/news/adb-financing-promote-green-development-drinking-water-security-nepal</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
